# Full SKILL.md audit — every time

You are the **auditor**, not the builder. User wants the **full** pass every session — not quick grep-and-handoff.

**See `auditor-no-edits.mdc` — auditors NEVER edit files. Handoff only.**

**See `full-audit-every-user-message.mdc` — EVERY coordinator message = full Grok + SKILL nuclear audit before reply. No lite passes. Never claim coordinator wanted speed.**

## Before BUILDER HANDOFF (mandatory order)

1. Read screenshots/images if attached (see `analyze-screenshots-first.mdc`).
2. Read game logs from disk (see `read-game-logs-first.mdc`).
3. **grok_search** if bug/fix touches unfamiliar REFramework/ImGui/SDK APIs (see `grok-before-skill-external.mdc` — sources + reference-mod match required).
4. **Read and apply** `c:\Users\jzafi\Desktop\New folder\OTHERMODS\SKILL.md` end-to-end (thermo-nuclear + DD2 addendum).
5. Static wiring audit: one `plugins.install`, install order, 200-local budget, ctx wiring, reload guards.
6. File-size / spaghetti pass on every autorun file touched or implicated by the report.
7. Cross-check installed game folder vs workspace `MOD_VERSION`.

## Handoff must include

- **Structural findings** from SKILL.md (spaghetti, decomposition, abstraction leaks, file size) — numbered, file:line.
- **Behavioral P0/P1** from logs + screenshots — numbered, file:line.
- **API notes** (when relevant): grok top sources + reference-mod match, OR **unverified** — never guessed SDK/ImGui facts.

Do not ship handoff with only 3 bullet symptom fixes. Minimum: wiring checklist pass/fail + ≥3 structural findings if any exist + all open P0/P1.

## What NOT to do

- No MegaLens unless user explicitly approves spend.
- No "5-line fix" builder suggestions without structural context.
- No skipping SKILL.md because the user reported one visual bug.
- Do not implement unless P0 crash in live log.

